    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset for a GWAS cohort of 10561 samples and 8777944 variants, including per-chromosome file sizing.",
    "rationale": "The binary .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte), so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome files use the same rule applied to each chromosome's variant count. The largest chromosome carries 1125341 variants. For a standard human GWAS panel this corresponds to 22 autosomes plus sex chromosomes (and optionally MT), giving 23-25 per-chromosome files.",
